{{Splduplicatenotes
| name = Spirit Siphon
| desc = Can be reapplied on the primary target, when {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} cast on the secondary target while the primary target is already affected by Spirit Siphon.
}}

 * {{Symbol|Charges}}
** Leveling the ability up grants {{#explode:{{#var:Spirit Siphon charges}}|/}} [[charge]] immediately.
** {{cf|shdnotes}} Acquiring the {{M|Aghanim's Shard|text=ability upgrade}} grants the additional charge immediately.

* The ability has three main components:
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|21px|1]] {{Symbol|Projectile|Link}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
*** {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|death_prophet_spirit_siphon_slow}}
**** Deals {{calc|v1*{{#var:Spirit Siphon basic1}}|v1={{#var:Spirit Siphon value2}}}} ({{Symbol|bonus t3l}} {{ValueColor||{{calc|v1*{{#var:Spirit Siphon basic1}}|v1={{#var:Spirit Siphon value2 tal}}}}|20tal}}) {{M|physical}} {{M|spell damage}} in {{#var:Spirit Siphon basic1}}-second intervals, starting {{#var:Spirit Siphon basic1}} upon debuff applifcation.
***** {{cf|talnotes}} The {{ValueColor||damage and heal increasing|20tal}} {{M|talent|t=t3l}} does not update the current instance.
***** {{cf|aghnotes}} Spawns an {{A|Death Prophet|Exorcism}} spirit of its corresponding level per ability cast, prioritizing {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} the unit-targeted enemy units.
**** Does not grant {{M|vision}}.
**** The link does not break when the debuff-affected enemy unit is affected by the following sources:
***** The {{M|Fog of War}}.
***** {{M|Invisible}} sources.
**** {{Symbol|fx|v}}
***** The ability effects visually draws to the location where the affected enemy unit was under {{M|vision}} previously.
**** Affects the following units:
***** {{M|Roshan}}
***** The {{M|Tormentor}}.
*** {{cf|shdnotes}} {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Fear}} {{Symbol|Fear|Run}} {{Symbol|Facing Angle|r}}
**** Applies a {{M|caster-fear}} on the affected enemy unit with the following properties:
***** {{Symbol|a|Counter}}
****** Procs at the {{ValueColor||{{#var:Spirit Siphon value5 shd}}rd|shd}} second of the link's duration, sourced to the {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|spirit_siphon_buff}} applied on Death Prophet upon ability cast.
****** Does not apply the fear component while the enemy is affected by the following source:
******* {{M|Hidden}} sources.
******* {{M|Invulnerable}} sources.
**** {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|death_prophet_spirit_siphon_fear}}
***** The {{M|fear}} component can only affect the same enemy unit once per cast.
***** Additionally applies the following ability effects to the debuff-affected enemy unit:
****** {{M|Cannot Act}}
****** {{M|Disarm}}
****** {{M|Muted}}
****** {{M|Silence}}
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|21px|2]] {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
*** Self-{{M|heals}} for the full value regardless of the damage instance value, in the same damage intervals, and does not continue to heal at full {{M|health}}.
*** {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|death_prophet_spirit_siphon}}
**** Casting the ability on another valid enemy unit, or on the same enemy, applies an independent buff on Death Prophet, with an independent ability intervals and duration.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-3.png|21px|3]] {{Symbol|Projectile|Linkbreak}}
*** The link breaks in the following conditions:
**** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|AffectedEnemyPosition - DeathProphetPosition > {{#var:Spirit Siphon value1}} , LinkBreak}}
**** Upon either the affected enemy's or Death Prophet's {{M|death}}.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Spirit Siphon icon0}}
| desc = Creates a spirit link between Death Prophet and an enemy unit, draining health from the enemy.
}}
* {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} + {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
** Deals {{calc|v1*{{#var:Spirit Siphon value4}}|v1={{#var:Spirit Siphon value2}}}} ({{Symbol|bonus t3l}} {{ValueColor||{{calc|v1*{{#var:Spirit Siphon value4}}|v1={{#var:Spirit Siphon value2 tal}}}}|20tal}}) damage ([[before reductions]]) and self-{{M|heals}} for the entire link duration.

* {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
** The ability effects are applied as follows:
**# The {{M|physical}} {{M|spell damage}} instance.
**# The self-{{M|heal}} instance.

